WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:05.300
BIS connects guided learning, real-world practice and evidence of what happened.

2
00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:10.854
The distinctive question: does a participant use what they learned when the facilitator is no longer beside them?

3
00:00:11.004 --> 00:00:14.590
Explore this fictional experience without creating an account.

4
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:23.773
Naledi is preparing job applications. She often reaches for her phone before she starts.

5
00:00:23.923 --> 00:00:29.306
She maps the pattern and chooses one smaller response: complete one application field first.

6
00:00:29.456 --> 00:00:35.499
Ten facilitated touchpoints support learning. The full Lab follows nine purposeful investigation stages.

7
00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:40.632
Predict how often the plan will be used, then record what actually happens.

8
00:00:40.782 --> 00:00:46.519
A day with no opportunity is valid evidence. It is excluded from the use-of-plan percentage.

9
00:00:46.669 --> 00:00:51.717
Predictions, observations, perceived control and reflection remain distinct.

10
00:00:54.200 --> 00:01:00.464
Lerato sees progress and support requests. Private reflection stays private until Naledi chooses to share.

11
00:01:00.614 --> 00:01:06.077
A facilitator acknowledges support and reviews shared evidence. Editing that evidence requires a fresh review.

12
00:01:06.227 --> 00:01:11.607
The participant’s evidence profile carries the plan, observations, interpretation and next action forward.

13
00:01:12.200 --> 00:01:17.770
Programme owners see aggregate findings, evidence coverage and practical follow-up questions.

14
00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:23.789
Choose a BIS programme, check the learning experience and share approved content with your group.

15
00:01:23.939 --> 00:01:29.483
This fixed fictional sample does not certify competence, employment outcomes or programme impact.
